WEBVTT

00:00.190 --> 00:02.680
Four robots share one delivery.

00:03.180 --> 00:08.350
The mailbag must travel from the shelf, through
the hatch, and onto the train.

00:08.970 --> 00:10.130
There’s a second job.

00:10.350 --> 00:11.670
Sign the delivery slip.

00:12.300 --> 00:14.450
Which robot can do each job?

00:15.330 --> 00:18.930
The orchestrator reads the depot’s knowledge
graph in Relate.

00:19.680 --> 00:22.860
Meet Jack, the forklift, and Patch, the
mechanic.

00:23.490 --> 00:25.490
Jack’s chassis supports lifting.

00:25.890 --> 00:29.010
With a working fork carriage mounted, he can
lift the tray.

00:29.810 --> 00:32.640
To sign the delivery slip, a robot scans it.

00:33.140 --> 00:35.340
Jack and Patch both have that skill.

00:35.930 --> 00:37.720
Only Jack can lift the tray.

00:38.180 --> 00:41.200
For the signature, the model can choose either
robot.

00:41.660 --> 00:42.820
It proposes a plan.

00:43.220 --> 00:46.220
The validator checks who can do each job,

00:46.280 --> 00:47.930
and what has to happen first.

00:48.410 --> 00:50.420
The approved plan goes into Relate.

00:52.070 --> 00:53.600
Watch the mailbag change hands.

00:54.350 --> 00:56.200
The executor updates the graph.

00:56.610 --> 00:58.690
That link now points to the courier.

01:01.830 --> 01:03.800
Then Jack’s fork carriage slips.

01:04.380 --> 01:06.100
The executor marks it offline.

01:06.810 --> 01:08.360
Loading needs those forks,

01:08.730 --> 01:10.820
and departure depends on loading.

01:11.370 --> 01:12.730
Signing can still go ahead.

01:15.050 --> 01:16.940
The orchestrator reads the changed graph.

01:17.630 --> 01:20.050
Patch has a driver that fits the broken collar.

01:20.570 --> 01:22.890
The model adds a repair before loading

01:23.180 --> 01:24.260
and keeps the signature.

01:25.910 --> 01:27.550
Jack signs with his scanner.

01:29.980 --> 01:31.340
Patch tightens the collar.

01:34.270 --> 01:35.720
Once the graph records the repair,

01:35.950 --> 01:37.150
Jack can load the bag.

01:39.530 --> 01:40.450
Both jobs are done.

01:40.940 --> 01:41.860
The train can leave.

01:43.410 --> 01:46.290
Now let’s follow the train into a bigger depot.

01:46.710 --> 01:48.750
Three deliveries, nine robots.

01:49.320 --> 01:51.540
The orchestrator runs the same graph query.

01:52.170 --> 01:53.790
The model proposes the plan.

01:54.210 --> 01:57.780
Relate shows which robot
can do each job, and when.
